      "writtenOn": "2025-03-31T19:12:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Here\u0027s my understanding of the relevant APIs:\n\nWhen the userspace calls `memref_create`, the kernel creates a ref-counted handle embedded into a `memref` struct. This handle can then be `mmap`ed. When the userspace `close`s the handle, or when the process exits, the ref count drops. When nothing references the `handle`, it is dropped and destroys the outer `memref` structure with it.\n\nTherefore, in this test, the clean up would happen on process exit. I assume that we have application-level APIs that indicate when Trusty is done using shared memory for actual TAs.\n\n@ahomescu@google.com, please correct me if I\u0027m wrong.",
